1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:01,820
Found sailing the Atlantic.

2
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:03,190
Nobody on board.

3
00:00:03,660 --> 00:00:04,840
You know the legend:

4
00:00:04,860 --> 00:00:07,020
warm tea, breakfast on the table.

5
00:00:07,240 --> 00:00:08,510
Most of that is fiction.

6
00:00:08,530 --> 00:00:09,430
Even the name.

7
00:00:09,860 --> 00:00:13,030
December 1872, east of the Azores.

8
00:00:13,050 --> 00:00:16,020
Another crew spots a ship drifting.

9
00:00:16,420 --> 00:00:17,430
The Mary Celeste.

10
00:00:17,450 --> 00:00:18,300
Her lifeboat:

11
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:18,670
gone.

12
00:00:19,090 --> 00:00:21,350
Six months of food and water still aboard.

13
00:00:21,650 --> 00:00:24,490
Seventeen hundred barrels of alcohol in the hold.

14
00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:27,960
A sounding rod lay on deck, as if someone had checked for

15
00:00:27,980 --> 00:00:28,510
leaks.

16
00:00:28,830 --> 00:00:30,740
Three and a half feet of water below.

17
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:32,020
Yet she was seaworthy.

18
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:34,280
So where did the warm tea come from?

19
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:40,410
In 1884, an anonymous magazine story renamed her Marie Celeste.

20
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:42,770
Many readers took it as fact.

21
00:00:42,790 --> 00:00:43,370
The author:

22
00:00:43,390 --> 00:00:46,330
Arthur Conan Doyle, before Sherlock Holmes.

23
00:00:46,730 --> 00:00:50,010
The cosy breakfast scenes came from retellings like these.

24
00:00:50,030 --> 00:00:51,180
Not from the ship.

25
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:53,330
The leading theories are ordinary.

26
00:00:53,570 --> 00:00:56,070
Alcohol fumes, and fear of an explosion.

27
00:00:56,320 --> 00:00:58,690
Or a broken pump, and fear she was sinking.

28
00:00:59,080 --> 00:01:02,140
Either way, they may have taken the lifeboat, and lost the ship.

29
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:07,130
Captain Briggs, his wife Sarah, two-year-old Sophia and seven crew were never

30
00:01:07,150 --> 00:01:07,630
found.

31
00:01:08,150 --> 00:01:09,000
Would you have left?

32
00:01:09,020 --> 00:01:09,920
Tell me below.

33
00:01:10,410 --> 00:01:13,220
After the last log entry, nine days passed.

34
00:01:13,240 --> 00:01:14,350
Until she was...
